(a) In the event that a quorum of the Board of Commissioners of Emanuel County becomes impossible to assemble due to injury of death of board members during an emergency or disaster, pursuant to O.C.G.A. § 38-3-50(f) there are hereby appointed the following emergency interim successors in descending order of succession:
(1) County administrator;
(2) County clerk;
(3) EMS director;
(4) County attorney;
(b) This section shall be construed and implemented in compliance with O.C.G.A. § 38-3-50, and any emergency interim successor designated by this section shall possess all authority provided for therein.
(c) Any meeting called for the purpose of deciding a local state of emergency, or any meeting held thereafter to consider matters relative to the State of Emergency, may be held by teleconference or other electronic means as may be required to obtain a quorum of the members of the board of commissioners.
(Ord. of 4-1-2020(1))

