The prohibitions of this article shall not apply to the following:
(1) Noises and/or sounds emanating from events sponsored or promoted by either the Emanuel County Board of Commission or any agency thereof or any municipality located within the corporate limits of Emanuel County or any agency thereof;
(2) Noises and/or sounds caused to be made by manufacturing, governmental, or industrial entities in the normal course of their business;
(3) Noises and/or sounds emanating from any official East Georgia State College event on East Georgia State College property or any official Emanuel County School District event on Emanuel County School District property;
(4) Noises or sounds made by domestic animals, provided, however, that said animals should not be allowed to disturb the comfort or repose of any persons in the vicinity by making long, continual, or frequent noise that shall in fact continue to be a violation of this article;
(5) Sound volumes produced by radio, tape player, or other mechanical sound making device or instrument from within a motor vehicle on a street or highway, which sound is controlled by the O.C.G.A. § 40-6-14;
(6) Noises or sounds made by law enforcement and other public safety officials performing their public functions;
(7) Noises or sounds made by the exploding of consumer fireworks on January 1, July 3, July 4, the first Monday in September, and December 31 of each year after 10:00 a.m. and up to and including the time of 11:59 p.m.; and on January 1 of each year beginning at the time of 12:00 midnight and up to and including the ending time of 1:00 a.m.
(Ord. of 12-16-2019(1))

